cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SymPhase in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "SymPhase: magnetic and spin-group symmetry, symmetry-allowed conductivity tensors and convex-hull phase stability for VASP"
abstract: >-
  SymPhase reads VASP calculations (POSCAR, INCAR, OUTCAR, OSZICAR) and determines the crystal
  and magnetic space groups and the non-relativistic spin group, classifying ferromagnets,
  antiferromagnets and altermagnets with their spin-splitting form. It derives the
  symmetry-allowed charge, spin and orbital conductivity tensors, separated into
  time-reversal-even and -odd parts, including unconventional spin-orbit-torque channels and
  the components that exist only with spin-orbit coupling. From a list of elements it collects
  the known phases (OQMD or Materials Project), builds the convex hull for any number of
  elements, writes VASP inputs with a SLURM job array and runs in parallel (multi-core or MPI).
type: software
